+## Separate owner-current basis when the native reader supplied no attribution/hash
+
+An entry may explicitly set `native_finding_basis: "in-flight-null-consumer-unobserved-owner-current-context-v1"`. Unknown basis values reject; entries without this field retain every exact-observation rule above unchanged. This second basis requires the original native finding to have **exactly** `subject_type:"in-flight-item"`, `consumer_id:null`, `observed_source:null`. Do not relabel it as the reader's direct-dependency observation. The entry instead supplies `owner_context_consumer_id`, `owner_current_source` and `owner_current_review`; it must not supply `consumer_id` or `observed_source` as though native attribution existed.
+
